      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Intersection vs Associate Table\nAn associate table is always an intersection table but not vice-versa.\nWhen an intersection table contains a field other than FK, it becomes\nan associate table, e.g. Enrollments table contains scores and grades.\nIn the same way, UserRoles is an intersection table.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Intersection vs Associate Table\nAn associate table is always an intersection table but not vice-versa.\nWhen an intersection table contains a field other than FK, it becomes\nan associate table, e.g. Enrollments table contains scores and grades.\nIn the same way, UserRoles is an intersection table.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
